 61FE    COULOMB EXCITATION            2009VA16                  15NDS    201503
 61FE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61FE2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61FE c  2009Va16: 2.87 MeV/nucleon beam of {+61}Mn was produced in fission of  
 61FE2c  uranium (uc{-x} target) induced by 1.4 GeV protons from ps Booster     
 61FE3c  at CERN. The laser ionized (rilis facility at ISOLDE-CERN) Mn          
 61FE4c  isotopes were extracted from the ion source and mass separated.        
 61FE5c  The 30-keV isobaric beam was bunched in a Penning trap (rextrap) and   
 61FE6c  injected in the electron beam ion source (ebis). The {+61}Mn beam      
 61FE7c  was accelerated to 2.87 MeV/nucleon and impinged on a {+109}Ag target. 
 61FE c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q) using miniball Ge detector array. Deduced    
 61FE2c  B(E2) value using gosia analysis. Comparison with shell-model          
 61FE3c  calculations. The data were normalized to excitations in the target    
 61FE4c  nucleus {+109}Ag.                                                      
